## Fix

The bug was in `advanceTurn` at `src/sim.ts:43`.

```diff
- if (foodSurplus >= 0) {
+ if (foodSurplus > 0) {
```

`foodSurplus` is `foodProduced - foodConsumed`. A settlement "barely breaking even" produces exactly as much food as its population consumes, so `foodSurplus === 0`. The old condition `>= 0` treated that break-even case as a surplus and grew the population by 1 each turn — which is exactly the runaway growth the playtesters reported.

Changing it to `> 0` means population only grows on a genuine food surplus, matching the function's documented contract ("grows by 1 if there was a food surplus this turn").


